---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const cards = [
  { id: 'restaurants', num: '01', img: '/images/hotels/luura-1.jpg', alt: 'A terrace above the sea at Luura, Paros',
    h: 'Dinner reservations', tag: 'The handful of Naousa tables worth planning around', meta: 'Booked · 3–6 weeks ahead in high season · Naousa fills even in October',
    desc: 'Paros eats better than islands twice as famous, and the reason is Naousa: a little Venetian harbor ringed with tables where the fishing boats are almost at your elbow, and lanes behind it where the best cooking on the island hides without a view. The catch is that everyone who&rsquo;s been knows it. Naousa books up even in October, so the tables that set the tone for a trip are a booking, not a walk-in. Tell me your dates and I&rsquo;ll arrange the nights that matter, working with your hotel&rsquo;s concierge where it helps.',
    notes: [
      ['Siparos, Santa Maria.', 'On the water looking across at Naxos, and the seafood benchmark on the island. This is the long first-night dinner that sets the tone for the trip, and the first table I go after.'],
      ['Yemeni, Naousa.', 'The best cooking on Paros plate for plate &mdash; modern Greek in the lanes behind the harbor, without a view and better for it.'],
      ['Sigi Ikthios, Naousa.', 'Tucked into the old harbor with the fishing boats almost at your table. The evening there is the point as much as the fish.'],
      ['Santa Pacou, Lefkes.', 'Dinner up in the marble village, a world away from the harbor scene. Timed after the sunset walk through Lefkes it&rsquo;s the most memorable evening on the island &mdash; and it belongs on your village day, below.'],
      ['Parostia at Cosme.', 'One of my favorite restaurants on Paros and the right last night. If you&rsquo;re staying at Cosme, it&rsquo;s an evening with nowhere to drive afterward.'],
      ['Mimi Kakushi at Luura.', 'New in August 2026: the Dubai contemporary-Japanese room&rsquo;s first Greek outpost, on a cliff facing the Antiparos sunset. Nothing else on Paros is attempting anything like it, and I expect it to be the hardest table on the island this season.'],
    ],
    take: 'One good rule: two big dinners across a four-night stay, and let the rest be long lunches &mdash; To Balconi tou Aki in Aliki is the one I&rsquo;d build a day around. Send me your dates and I&rsquo;ll tell you which nights are already tight and what I can still get.' },
  { id: 'antiparos', num: '02', img: '/images/excursions/paros/a3b0ba92.jpg', alt: 'A catamaran anchored in clear water off Antiparos',
    h: 'Your day on the water', tag: 'The Antiparos sail, booked before it goes', meta: 'Best for · couples, anyone who came for the water, groups of up to ten',
    desc: 'The water on the Antiparos side of Paros is the clearest I know in the Cyclades, and the only way to reach the best of it is by boat. The sails run out of Piso Livadi on the east coast &mdash; a working fishing harbor twenty minutes from Naousa, with none of the marina scrum you get on the bigger islands. This is the one booking on Paros I&rsquo;d protect, because the good boats and the good weather windows both go first.',
    notes: [
      ['Sail to Antiparos &amp; Despotiko.', 'The full day. Out of Piso Livadi under sail at 9:30, down into the Antiparos Strait, anchored in the Blue Lagoon, then right around South Antiparos with a full lunch cooked and served on deck, and a last swim off South Paros on the way home. Fully private for the two of you, or shared with up to ten &mdash; your call.'],
      ['The evening sail.', 'The shorter version, and lovely on its own night: sails up at 6:00pm, a drink in hand, a swim in a sheltered bay, then dinner served on deck as the sun drops. Back at the dock by dusk, so it never collides with a table in Naousa.'],
      ['A private boat, priced for the boat.', 'Three boats run the private days, and the rate is for the whole boat rather than per person &mdash; the same whether it&rsquo;s the two of you or a full group, with skipper, fuel and VAT included. I&rsquo;ll match the boat to your budget rather than the other way around.'],
      ['Antiparos, the easy way.', 'If the sail isn&rsquo;t your day, the little car ferry shuttles from Pounda every half hour and takes ten minutes. No booking, no drama &mdash; one long main street of galleries and good tavernas, the cave in the hills above, and Soros beach on the way back.'],
      ['The Meltemi is real.', 'Summer wind can move a sail with little notice, so I place the boat early in your stay with room to shift it &mdash; which you can&rsquo;t do once you&rsquo;ve prepaid a fixed date online.'],
    ],
    take: 'Tell me your dates and who&rsquo;s coming and I&rsquo;ll hold the right boat for the right morning. The full menu, with what each one costs, is in my <a href="/paros-excursions.html">Paros excursions guide</a>.' },
  { id: 'beaches', num: '03', img: '/images/islands/paros-days.jpg', alt: 'A lounger at the water&rsquo;s edge on Paros',
    h: 'Beaches &amp; down days', tag: 'Choose the beach by mood, not by whichever one your hotel sits on', meta: 'Best for · slow days, long lunches, a break from the car',
    desc: 'This is why Paros over the bigger names: beaches you choose by mood rather than by geography, and none of them more than forty minutes from anywhere else. Nothing here needs more than the car and a loose sense of when lunch should be &mdash; but the ones with beds are still worth reserving in July and August, and I&rsquo;d rather you didn&rsquo;t find that out at eleven in the morning.',
    notes: [
      ['Kolymbithres.', 'Wind-carved granite coves and water you can see straight through &mdash; unlike any other beach in the Cyclades, and a short hop across the bay from Naousa. Go early, before the boats arrive.'],
      ['Crios Beach Club.', 'The island&rsquo;s most relaxed beachfront setting for swimming and a slow lunch. Nothing to do but stay put until the light changes &mdash; the day that asks nothing of you at all, and the beds I reserve first.'],
      ['Lageri and Santa Maria.', 'Lageri for calm, shallow water and almost nobody on it; Santa Maria when you want loungers and a bar. Both face Naxos across the channel, and both are ten minutes from Naousa.'],
      ['If you&rsquo;re at Cosme or Par&imacr;lio, you already have one.', 'Cosme&rsquo;s private beach club sits directly in front of the hotel, and Par&imacr;lio guests use it for free &mdash; some of the best days on Paros are the ones where you never leave.'],
    ],
    take: 'One rule for Paros: rent the car for every day you&rsquo;re there. Roads are good, parking is easy outside the two towns, and the best beaches sit at the end of short dirt tracks. I&rsquo;ll have it waiting at the airport or the port.' },
];
---
<Layout
  canonical="already-booked-paros.html"
  title="Already Booked Paros? Start Here | Suites With Keith"
  description="Send me the booking details for the hotel you already reserved. I'll have my perks added — no changes to your reservation — and build the rest of the trip around it: the Naousa tables, the Antiparos sail, the car, the ferries."
  preload="/images/islands/paros-hero.jpg"
>

<!-- hero -->
<header class="hero" style="min-height:min(76svh,700px);">
  <img class="hero-img" src="/images/islands/paros-hero.jpg" alt="The granite coves at Kolymbithres, Paros" width="1200" height="1800" fetchpriority="high" />
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Paros &middot; already booked</p>
    <h1 class="display-xl" style="margin-top:18px;">Already booked<br><em>your hotel?</em></h1>
    <p class="sub">Send me the booking details for the hotel you already reserved. I&rsquo;ll have my perks added &mdash; no changes to your reservation &mdash; and then I&rsquo;ll build the rest of the trip around it: the Naousa tables, the Antiparos sail, the car, the ferries.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn" href="#inquire" data-gtag-label="send_reservations" data-gtag-location="hero">Send me your booking details</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- intro -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container ab-intro">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="deck" style="max-width:46ch;">Keep the room you booked. Send me the confirmation, and I&rsquo;ll add my perks to it and build the rest of Paros around it.</p>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:20px; max-width:58ch;">First, the part most people don&rsquo;t know: you don&rsquo;t have to have booked through me to get my perks. Send me the booking details for the hotel you already reserved and I&rsquo;ll have them added &mdash; a space-available upgrade, daily breakfast, a hotel credit, whatever the property extends to my clients &mdash; with no changes to your existing reservation. Same room, same dates, same rate.</p>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:14px; max-width:58ch;">Then the real work starts, because the hotel is the easy part. The Naousa table that was full even in October, the Antiparos sail that went to someone else, the Athens flight that sold out weeks before the ferries did. That&rsquo;s the part I take on too. With your confirmation and your dates I&rsquo;ll come back with a plan for the days around it &mdash; the handful of tables worth planning around held before you land, a boat out of Piso Livadi on the right morning, the car sorted, and transfers that account for what the Aegean does in August.</p>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:14px; max-width:58ch;">Paros is the island I recommend more every year, and I spent my time there the way I&rsquo;d want you to &mdash; eating, sailing, and driving to the villages and beaches that make it the Cyclades beyond the postcard. None of this comes off a list. Still deciding on the hotel? Start with my <a href="/paros.html" style="color:var(--brass);">Paros guide</a> or <a href="/cosme-vs-parilio-paros.html" style="color:var(--brass);">Cosme or Par&imacr;lio</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal" style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px;">
      <p class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass);">How it works</p>
      <div style="margin-bottom:22px;">
        <p class="ab-note"><b>01 &middot; Send me the booking details</b> <span>for the hotel you&rsquo;ve already reserved &mdash; or just forward the confirmation email.</span></p>
        <p class="ab-note"><b>02 &middot; I have my perks added.</b> <span>No changes to your existing reservation &mdash; same room, same dates, same rate.</span></p>
        <p class="ab-note"><b>03 &middot; I build the rest of the trip around it.</b> <span>Everything below.</span></p>
      </div>
      <p class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass);">What I handle</p>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#inquire"><b>Send me your booking details &rarr;</b></a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#restaurants">Dinner reservations</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#antiparos">Your day on the water</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#beaches">Beaches &amp; down days</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#village-day">The village day</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#athens">Athens add-on</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#extensions">Santorini &amp; Milos extensions</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#logistics">Transfers &amp; ferries</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{cards.map((c, i) => (
  <section class={`section${i % 2 === 0 ? ' band on-shadow' : ''}`} id={c.id} style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class={`ab-grid${i % 2 ? ' flip' : ''}`}>
        <figure class="reveal ab-media">
          <img src={c.img} alt={c.alt} width="1800" height="1300" loading={i === 0 ? 'eager' : 'lazy'} decoding="async" style={c.imgStyle} />
        </figure>
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="stamp plain" style={`font-weight:700; color:${i % 2 === 0 ? 'var(--brass-lit)' : 'var(--brass)'};`}>No. {c.num}</span>
          <h2 class="display-l" style="margin-top:12px;" set:html={c.h} />
          <p class="deck" style="margin-top:10px; font-size:1.05rem;" set:html={c.tag} />
          <p class="stamp plain ab-meta" set:html={c.meta} />
          <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:18px;" set:html={c.desc} />
          <div style="margin-top:22px;">
            {c.notes.map(([b, t]) => <p class="ab-note"><b set:html={b} /> <span set:html={t} /></p>)}
          </div>
          <div class="verdict" style="margin-top:26px;"><p class="ab-take" set:html={c.take} /></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
))}

<!-- easiest way to start -->
<section class="section" style="padding:64px 0;">
  <div class="container ab-callout reveal">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow" style="display:block; margin-bottom:12px;">The easiest way to start</span>
      <h3 class="display-m">Send me your booking details</h3>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:12px; max-width:52ch;">Your hotel confirmation and your dates are enough. I&rsquo;ll have my perks added to the reservation you already have &mdash; nothing about it changes &mdash; and come back with what I&rsquo;d book around it, and what&rsquo;s already getting tight on your nights.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn" href="#inquire">Send your booking details</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- the village day -->
<section class="section band on-shadow" id="village-day" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">The village day</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">The day Paros does better than any island I know</h2>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:16px; max-width:62ch;">Real villages with real life in them, a mountain in the middle, and a seafood lunch on the south coast between them. This is the day I&rsquo;d build first &mdash; in the right order, with the two tables held before you land.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ab-wine">
      <figure class="reveal" style="margin:0;">
        <img src="/images/hotels/parilio-1.jpg" alt="Whitewashed Cycladic architecture at Par&imacr;lio, Paros" width="1800" height="1201" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="width:100%; aspect-ratio:4/5; object-fit:cover;" />
      </figure>
      <div class="ledger reveal" style="border-top:1px solid var(--band-hairline);">
        <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">01</span><span class="d"><b>Lefkes, in the morning.</b> Start in the mountain village &mdash; marble lanes, no sea, no crowds. Wander before the day heats up, and save the sunset for the drive back. <span class="ab-wmeta">Marble lanes &middot; around 10:00am</span></span></div>
        <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">02</span><span class="d"><b>Lunch at To Balconi tou Aki, Aliki.</b> South to the fishing village of Aliki for a seafood lunch at one of my favorite tavernas on the island &mdash; the lunch I&rsquo;d build the whole day around. <span class="ab-wmeta">Seafood on the water &middot; around 1:30pm</span></span></div>
        <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">03</span><span class="d"><b>A swim at Lageri.</b> Calm, shallow, clear water and almost nobody on it. The afternoon that asks nothing of you. <span class="ab-wmeta">Calm water &middot; the afternoon</span></span></div>
        <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">04</span><span class="d"><b>Back up to Lefkes for Santa Pacou.</b> Time it after the sunset walk through the marble streets and it&rsquo;s the most memorable evening on the island. This is the table I hold before you land. <span class="ab-wmeta">Booked ahead &middot; sunset, then dinner</span></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="verdict reveal" style="margin-top:40px; max-width:640px; border-left-color:var(--brass-lit);">
      <p>This is the day the rental car earns its keep &mdash; you drive it, at your own pace. I hold the two tables, put it on the day the wind is least likely to cooperate with a boat, and give you the route in the order that works.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- athens add-on -->
<section class="section" id="athens" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="ab-grid">
      <figure class="reveal ab-media">
        <img src="/images/islands/athens-hero.jpg" alt="Athens at dusk" width="1800" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </figure>
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass);">No. 04</span>
        <h2 class="display-l" style="margin-top:12px;">The Athens add-on</h2>
        <p class="deck" style="margin-top:10px; font-size:1.05rem;">Two or three nights, not a layover</p>
        <p class="stamp plain ab-meta">Best for · bookending the trip, food lovers, first-time Greece</p>
        <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:18px;">Most people treat Athens as a gateway to the islands. I think that&rsquo;s a mistake. Give yourself two or three nights and you&rsquo;ll discover one of Europe&rsquo;s most exciting food cities, incredible luxury hotels, and neighborhoods that feel completely different from one another. It&rsquo;s the perfect way to begin or end a trip through Greece.</p>
        <div style="margin-top:22px;">
          <p class="ab-note"><b>Put it at the end, not the beginning.</b> <span>Flying home out of Athens gives you a buffer against a cancelled ferry or a delayed island flight &mdash; and you arrive in the city already unwound.</span></p>
          <p class="ab-note"><b>Two nights is the minimum that works.</b> <span>One night is an airport hotel with extra steps. Three is genuinely great.</span></p>
          <p class="ab-note"><b>Book the Acropolis early.</b> <span>Timed entry, and the first slot of the morning is the only one worth having in summer.</span></p>
        </div>
        <div class="verdict" style="margin-top:26px;"><p class="ab-take">Read the full <a href="/athens.html">Athens guide</a> for where I&rsquo;d stay and how I&rsquo;d spend the days.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- extensions -->
<section class="section" id="extensions" style="padding-top:0; scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Santorini &amp; Milos extensions</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">Add one island, not three</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="cards reveal" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr)); max-width:760px;">
      <a class="card" href="/santorini.html">
        <img src="/images/islands/santorini-hero.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="object-position:center bottom;" />
        <div class="pad"><span class="kicker">The Cyclades</span><h3>Santorini</h3><p>The classic pairing &mdash; Paros first, then the caldera as the finale. Roughly two hours by high-speed boat, or a helicopter.</p><span class="go">Read the guide &rarr;</span></div>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/milos.html">
        <img src="/images/islands/milos-hero.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <div class="pad"><span class="kicker">The Cyclades</span><h3>Milos</h3><p>The swimming island &mdash; volcanic cliffs, Kleftiko by boat, and Er&#275;ma, from the same group as Cosme and Par&imacr;lio.</p><span class="go">Read the guide &rarr;</span></div>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="verdict reveal" style="margin-top:36px; max-width:640px;">
      <p>Paros is four nights for most people. Paros then Santorini is the eating trip on my <a href="/greek-island-pairings.html" style="color:var(--brass);">pairings page</a>; Paros then Milos is the one I&rsquo;d build for anyone who wants to be in the water every day. Either way, two islands per week &mdash; three in seven nights is really three travel days &mdash; and I can arrange a private boat or helicopter between them if the ferry schedules don&rsquo;t cooperate.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- logistics -->
<section class="section band on-shadow" id="logistics" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container ab-log">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-head" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
        <span class="eyebrow">Getting there &amp; around</span>
        <h2 class="display-l" style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.2rem);">Airport &amp; ferry logistics</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="kv">
        <div class="kv-row ab-row"><dt style="color:var(--band-ash);">Arriving</dt><dd style="color:var(--band-ink);">Fly Athens &rarr; PAS, forty minutes &middot; ferry into Parikia &middot; private boat transfer &middot; private helicopter</dd></div>
        <div class="kv-row ab-row"><dt style="color:var(--band-ash);">Getting around</dt><dd style="color:var(--band-ink);">Rental car for the whole stay &middot; private transfers &middot; the Pounda car ferry to Antiparos</dd></div>
        <div class="kv-row ab-row"><dt style="color:var(--band-ash);">What I arrange</dt><dd style="color:var(--band-ink);">Private transfers between the airport, Parikia port and your hotel, the car, and the boats &mdash; plus helicopters through my <a href="/hoper.html" style="color:var(--brass-lit);">Hoper partnership</a> and private boats for island combinations. Flights into Paros sell out well before the ferries do in season, so the Athens leg is the first thing I lock in.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div style="margin-top:20px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px;">
        <a class="toc-link" style="color:var(--brass-lit);" href="/greek-ferry-rules.html">5 Greek ferry rules every couple should know &rarr;</a>
        <a class="toc-link" style="color:var(--brass-lit);" href="/paros-excursions.html">The Paros excursions guide &rarr;</a>
        <a class="toc-link" style="color:var(--brass-lit);" href="/private-boat-transfers.html">Private boat transfers between islands &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass-lit); margin-bottom:16px;">Rules I&rsquo;d give any client</p>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Book the flight before the ferry.</b> Paros&rsquo; airport is small, and the Athens flights sell out well before the boats do in season.</div>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Never book the last ferry of the day.</b> If it cancels, there&rsquo;s nothing behind it.</div>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Don&rsquo;t fly home the same day you sail.</b> Build in a night. The Aegean does not care about your itinerary.</div>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Two islands per week. That&rsquo;s the limit.</b> Three islands in seven nights is three travel days.</div>
      <div class="verdict" style="margin-top:30px; border-left-color:var(--brass-lit);">
        <p>You&rsquo;ve done the hard part by choosing the hotel. Send me the confirmation, keep the reservation exactly as it is, and let me handle the rest of it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- the form -->
<section class="section inquire" id="inquire" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow reveal" style="display:block; margin-bottom:16px;">Send me your booking details</span>
    <h2 class="display-l reveal">Your confirmation and dates are enough to start</h2>
    <p class="deck reveal" style="margin:18px auto 0; max-width:38ch;">I&rsquo;ll add my perks and build the rest.</p>
    <form class="inquire-form reveal" action="https://formspree.io/f/mjgnadov" method="POST" style="max-width:520px;">
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="Already Booked Paros — reservation details" />
      <input type="hidden" name="page" value="already-booked-paros" />
      <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
      <label for="ab-name">Name</label>
      <input id="ab-name" type="text" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
      <label for="ab-email">Email</label>
      <input id="ab-email" type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
      <label for="ab-hotel">Hotel you booked</label>
      <input id="ab-hotel" type="text" name="hotel" placeholder="Par&imacr;lio" autocomplete="off" />
      <label for="ab-dates">Travel dates</label>
      <input id="ab-dates" type="text" name="travel_dates" placeholder="September 2027, 4 nights" autocomplete="off" />
      <label for="ab-details">Confirmation number, and anything else &mdash; rough is fine</label>
      <input id="ab-details" type="text" name="details" placeholder="Conf. 4821XX &middot; honeymoon &middot; want the Antiparos sail" autocomplete="off" />
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Send my booking details</button>
      <p class="note">Rather just forward the confirmation email? Send it to keith.pence@fora.travel &mdash; that&rsquo;s the fastest way to get the perks added.</p>
      <p class="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
    <p class="small reveal" style="margin-top:26px; color:var(--ash);">Nothing about your reservation changes &mdash; same room, same dates, same rate. The perks and the planning are on top. Haven&rsquo;t locked in the hotel yet? Start with <a href="/paros.html" style="color:var(--brass);">the Paros guide</a> or <a href="/cosme-vs-parilio-paros.html" style="color:var(--brass);">Cosme or Par&imacr;lio</a> &mdash; the island&rsquo;s two best hotels, head to head.</p>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .toc-link { font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--brass); text-decoration: none; }
  .toc-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .ab-intro { display: grid; gap: 44px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: start; }
